# "Can the monitoring server itself see the network?" reference targets
# (`vantage_points`), pinged by the "vantage-points" job. If EVERY one is
# unreachable the problem is the server's own network path: the
# MonitoringVantageLost alert fires and Alertmanager holds back the
# per-device alerts (prometheus/rules/vantage.yml, inhibit_rules).
#
# Pick targets on the SERVER'S side of the network that you do not want paged
# on as "down" themselves: the server's default gateway, and optionally a
# public address. A second independent target makes a false "network lost"
# less likely.
{% for v in vantage_points %}
- targets: [{{ v.ip | string | to_json }}]
  labels:
    vantage: {{ v.vantage | string | to_json }}
{% endfor %}
